# Line endings are a property of this repository, not of whoever clones it.
#
# The build writes CRLF and the checks compare bytes, so a working copy that
# checks out with LF makes the first rebuild rewrite every page. Measured on
# 2026-09-12: a clone with core.autocrlf unset, rebuilt with nothing changed,
# produced a 1700 line diff across 26 files, and all five checks still passed.
# Without this file the result depends on each machine's git config, which a
# new owner has no reason to have set the way this one does.
#
# Blobs stay LF in every case. These rules govern the working copy only.

* text=auto eol=crlf

# The four files the build neither reads nor writes, kept as they are stored so
# adding this file changes nothing in an existing working copy.
.gitignore text eol=lf
.env.example text eol=lf
CLAUDE.md text eol=lf

# GitHub Pages reads this one itself to resolve the custom domain, and the
# generator emits it with a single bare LF for that reason. A clone that turned
# it into CRLF would hand a new owner a domain file unlike the one that works.
/docs/CNAME text eol=lf

# Copied into the output byte for byte rather than rendered, so it ships as it
# is stored.
*.svg text eol=lf

# Never touched, whatever a platform's text detection would guess.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.webp binary
*.ico binary
*.woff binary
*.woff2 binary
